Implement complete ConvertDDSToTexture() method (PRD lines 376-392):
```csharp
public static ImageTexture ConvertDDSToTexture(byte[] ddsData)
{
    using var decoder = new BcDecoder();
    var ddsFile = DdsFile.Load(new MemoryStream(ddsData));

    // Support DXT1, DXT3, DXT5 compression formats
    var pixelData = decoder.DecodeToPixelsRgba32(ddsFile);

    var image = Image.CreateFromData(
        ddsFile.Header.Width,
        ddsFile.Header.Height,
        false,
        Image.Format.Rgba8,
        pixelData.AsSpan().AsBytes().ToArray()
    );

    return ImageTexture.CreateFromImage(image);
}
```

Key requirements:
- Use BCnEncoder.Net library for DDS decoding
- Support DXT1, DXT3, DXT5 compression formats commonly used in game assets
- Convert decoded pixel data to Godot's Image.Format.Rgba8
- Create ImageTexture from converted Image data
- Implement texture caching mechanism to avoid redundant conversions
- Handle error cases for unsupported DDS formats gracefully

Reference Godot ImageTexture documentation: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_imagetexture.html

Create DMapEditorDock.cs in addons/dmap_importer/Editor/ following PRD lines 408-456. Based on EditorPlugin dock example from Godot documentation.

**Complete Implementation (PRD lines 408-456):**
```csharp
#if TOOLS
using Godot;

[Tool]
public partial class DMapEditorDock : Control
{
    private DMapRenderer currentMap;
    private SpinBox heightEditor;
    private OptionButton surfaceSelector;
    private CheckBox walkableToggle;

    public override void _Ready()
    {
        CustomMinimumSize = new Vector2(250, 0);

        var vbox = new VBoxContainer();
        AddChild(vbox);

        // Tile properties section
        vbox.AddChild(new Label() { Text = "Tile Properties" });

        // Height editor (from Tile.Height)
        heightEditor = new SpinBox();
        heightEditor.MinValue = -100;
        heightEditor.MaxValue = 100;
        heightEditor.ValueChanged += OnHeightChanged;
        vbox.AddChild(heightEditor);

        // Surface type (from Tile.Surface)
        surfaceSelector = new OptionButton();
        surfaceSelector.AddItem("Grass");
        surfaceSelector.AddItem("Stone");
        surfaceSelector.AddItem("Water");
        surfaceSelector.Selected += OnSurfaceChanged;
        vbox.AddChild(surfaceSelector);

        // Walkable toggle (from Tile.NoAccess)
        walkableToggle = new CheckBox();
        walkableToggle.Text = "Walkable";
        walkableToggle.Toggled += OnWalkableToggled;
        vbox.AddChild(walkableToggle);
    }

    private void OnHeightChanged(double value)
    {
        // Update selected tile's height
        if (currentMap != null)
        {
            var selectedTile = GetSelectedTile();
            UpdateTileProperty(selectedTile, "height", (int)value);
        }
    }
}
#endif
```

**Key Features:**
- Extends Control with CustomMinimumSize (250x0)
- VBoxContainer layout with "Tile Properties" label
- SpinBox for height editing (-100 to 100 range, maps to Tile.Height)
- OptionButton for surface types (Grass/Stone/Water, maps to Tile.Surface)
- CheckBox for walkability toggle (maps to Tile.NoAccess inverse)
- Signal connections for real-time updates
- GetSelectedTile() and UpdateTileProperty() methods for editor integration
- Proper #if TOOLS directive and [Tool] attribute

**Additional Implementation Requirements:**
- Complete OnSurfaceChanged and OnWalkableToggled signal handlers
- Implement GetSelectedTile() method to identify selected tile
- Implement UpdateTileProperty() method for live updates
- Integrate with DMapRenderer for current map reference
- Add proper error handling and validation
